### Crash Report

crash-2026-10-21_15.26.56-client.txt: https://p.kdan.dev/haL1C6V

### Steps to Reproduce the Crash

**JEI versions:** jei-26.3-fabric-31.9.0.58 and 31.9.0.61
**Minecraft:** 26.3 (Fabric)

## What happens
With JEI and a mod that adds Nether biomes through Fabric API's `NetherBiomes.addNetherBiome` (in our case BetterNether), joining a world disconnects the player while the client handles `ClientboundUpdateRecipesPacket`.

31.9.0.58:
```
[Render thread/ERROR]: Failed to handle packet ClientboundUpdateRecipesPacket[...]
java.lang.IllegalStateException: Errors during registry creation
    at net.minecraft.core.RegistrySetBuilder$BuildState.throwOnError(RegistrySetBuilder.java:125)
    at net.minecraft.core.RegistrySetBuilder.build(RegistrySetBuilder.java:210)
    at net.minecraft.data.registries.VanillaRegistries.createWorldLookup(VanillaRegistries.java:190)
    at mezz.jei.common.util.RegistryUtil.createRegistryProvider(RegistryUtil.java:65)
    at mezz.jei.common.util.RegistryUtil.getRegistryProvider(RegistryUtil.java:53)
    at mezz.jei.fabric.platform.ItemStackHelper.createFuelContext(ItemStackHelper.java:49)
    at mezz.jei.fabric.platform.ItemStackHelper.getFuelProperties(ItemStackHelper.java:34)
    at mezz.jei.library.plugins.vanilla.cooking.fuel.FuelRecipeMaker.lambda$getFuelRecipes$0(FuelRecipeMaker.java:21)
    ...
    at mezz.jei.library.plugins.vanilla.VanillaPlugin.registerRecipes(VanillaPlugin.java:368)
    Suppressed: java.lang.IllegalStateException: No value registered for key betternether:old_warped_woods
    Suppressed: java.lang.IllegalStateException: No value registered for key betternether:nether_jungle
    ... (one per modded Nether biome)
[Render thread/WARN]: Client disconnected with reason: Network Protocol Error
```

31.9.0.61 fails the same way, through `ClientCookingFuelRegistryProvider.create(ClientCookingFuelRegistryProvider.java:46)` → `VanillaRegistries.createWorldLookup()`.

## Cause
As far as we can tell, JEI for 26.3 adds the registry set from `VanillaRegistries.createWorldLookup()` to the client's registries to build the fuel `LootContext`. That runs vanilla's registry bootstrap on the modded client which includes baking the `minecraft:nether` multi-noise parameter list. Fabric API's `NetherBiomePresetMixin` (fabric-biome-api-v1) adds every biome registered through `NetherBiomes.addNetherBiome` to that bake. Since those biomes are defined in datapacks, they don't exist in the vanilla-only registry set making`RegistrySetBuilder` fail on unbound holders.

We think this isn't specific to one mod: any mod that uses `NetherBiomes.addNetherBiome` hits it (see the reproduction below). 

## Reproduction
Minimal mod, nothing but Fabric API: one datapack biome (`data/jeirepro/worldgen/biome/test_nether.json`, a copy of vanilla's `nether_wastes`), registered from `onInitialize` exactly as Fabric documents it:

