For AppleCore, I am currently doing some ugly hackery to retrieve the currently hovered stack from JEI. It'd be nice to have a single API method that would return the hovered ItemStack from any of the currently applicable JEI Gui elements (ItemListOverlay, GuiRecipes, etc). From what I can tell, InputHandler currently has some methods similar to this, but none are available through the API.

Barring that, adding a `getStackUnderMouse` method to `IRecipesGui` (a la `IItemListOverlay`) would also make getting the ItemStack fairly easy. Then I'd be able to do something like:

``` java
GuiScreen curScreen = Minecraft.getMinecraft().currentScreen;
ItemStack hoveredStack = null;

if (curScreen instanceof IRecipesGui)
{
    hoveredStack = ((IRecipesGui) curScreen).getStackUnderMouse()
}
if (hoveredStack == null)
{
    IItemListOverlay overlay = runtime.getItemListOverlay();
    hoveredStack = overlay.getStackUnderMouse();
}
```

Let me know if I'm missing something that makes this already possible.

